// result_end
\caption(Explicit 5-epoch Adam fit of PyramidNet-20 and a tensor-computed true/predicted-class count matrix at the selected checkpoint. Training uses augmentation and batch BN moments; validation/test use saved moving moments. Counts sum to 64; IDs follow the original CIFAR-10 order.)
\alttext(Explicit 5-epoch Adam fit of PyramidNet-20 and a tensor-computed true/predicted-class count matrix at the selected checkpoint. Training uses augmentation and batch BN moments; validation/test use saved moving moments. Counts sum to 64; IDs follow the original CIFAR-10 order.)


The selected epoch is 4: validation NLL 2.196306, inference training NLL 1.704807,
and test NLL 2.097574 with accuracy 0.218750. Validation and test NLL sit only a little
below the uniform-guess value ln 10 ≈ 2.303, and validation rises again at epoch 5, so
the falling training loss does not yet translate into reliable generalization.
The training trace uses augmented images and batch moments, while the validation
and restored inference losses use moving moments. These results support the
worked optimization procedure, not a published-performance claim.

> Native confusion matrices

These matrices use the held-out predictions from the executed program above.
The native `ConfusionMatrix` SVG API labels exact counts with true classes
running from top to bottom and predicted classes from left to right.

\image(figures/pyramidnet_confusion_api_0.svg)
\caption(Held-out classification confusion counts, evaluation 1. Exact cell counts are printed in the image.)
\alttext(Integer prediction counts with true classes as rows and predicted classes as columns.)


> Conclusion

Gradual widening changes every unit's budget, while parameter-free shortcuts preserve signed
signals through pooling and zero extension. Explicit geometry, gradient and optimization checks
show how that design behaves in a complete tensor classifier.

> References

- [Han et al. (2017), Deep Pyramidal Residual Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.02915).
- [Authors' implementation](https://github.com/jhkim89/PyramidNet/blob/master/addpyramidnet.lua).
- [CIFAR-10 dataset](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html).
